From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Linux app windows take the focus as on a Linux
 desktop

ChromeOS shows every window of the default Wayland server's clients
inactive unless Chrome granted it permission (ARC, or Crostini windows
for five seconds after the app is launched again). On NickelOS those
clients are the user's Linux apps on the device, so a dialog an app
opened (a save dialog, its password prompt) and the polkit password
prompt came up without the keyboard: typing went on into the window
behind.

- ChromeSecurityDelegate::CanSelfActivate: a window takes the focus when
  it first shows; later an app may move the focus between its own windows
  (a dialog for the window in use, or another window with the same app
  id), never take it from another app's window. Permissions Chrome grants
  still apply.
- Exo gains xdg-activation-v1, which GTK and Qt use to hand the focus on
  (gtk_window_present, an app started from another): tokens are good only
  when asked for from the window that has the focus, for one use within
  ten seconds; without a good token, an activation is the app's own
  request and the security delegate decides (so an app started again from
  the launcher brings its open window forward, through the permission the
  shelf already grants).

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ash/exo/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ash/exo/BUILD.gn
